// =============================================================================
// tidelink_top_full_asic_v2.flist — S3 PHY-swap build variant (V2)
//
// V2 = the NEW shared GPIO-PHY component (deps/tidelink-phy, the
// silicon-validated FIX-N..R serdes fork + new lane-mask-aware calibrator)
// in place of the V1 local_overrides/tidelink-gpio-phy composition.
//
// The new component's serdes forks share module names with the V1 sources
// (WavD2DGpio, WavD2DGpioRx, WavD2DGpioTx, WlinkGPIOPHY, tidelink_lane_deskew,
// tidelink_phy_align_calibrator, tidelink_lane_checker*) so the two trees
// CANNOT co-compile — V2 is selected by compiling THIS flist, which:
//   1. defines TIDELINK_PHY_V2 (activates the `ifdef arms in the shared RTL:
//      src/rtl/local_overrides/Wlink.v, axi_chiplet_controller.sv and
//      src/rtl/tidelink_top.sv);
//   2. swaps the serdes/deskew/calibrator/checker sources to
//      deps/tidelink-phy/rtl;
//   3. adds the PHY-owned TX/RX lane front-end blocks the new WavD2DGpio
//      instantiates (tx_segmenter / tx_mask / rx_demask);
//   4. drops src/rtl/tidelink_eye_regs.sv (eye-vis retired in V2, AUDIT #17 —
//      Region 10 APB reads return 0 via the tidelink_top RAZ tie).
//
// The V1 flist (tidelink_top_full_asic.flist) MUST NOT be edited as part of
// this change: with TIDELINK_PHY_V2 undefined every shared-RTL `ifdef arm
// compiles the old code, keeping the default V1 build bit-identical.
//
// tidelink_phy_sync_insert IS now included (2026-06-15): the DEFAULT-OFF LL
// re-hunt beacon inserter sits in the WavD2DGpio TX path, gated by APB
// SWI_SYNC_INSERT_EN (Region 8 slot 0 bit[2], 0x4403_2100) which resets 0 ->
// pure passthrough / bit-identical until SW opts in. tidelink_phy_sync_detect IS
// now included (2026-07): the WavD2DGpio_v2 local override instantiates it
// unconditionally as a read-only post-deskew SYNC obs (mirrors obs_sync_detected_cnt);
// the source line below is REQUIRED or the V2 ASIC elaborate dies on the undefined
// module. NOT included (deliberate): tidelink_gpio_phy_rx/tx wrappers and the BIST
// files — the silicon-proven composition (PHY-BIST core) puts the checker +
// calibrator at controller level on the 128-bit link data.
// =============================================================================
+define+TIDELINK_PHY_V2
+incdir+${TIDELINK_HOME}/src/rtl
+incdir+${TIDELINK_HOME}/src/rtl/fifo
+incdir+${TIDELINK_HOME}/deps/tidelink-phy/rtl

